# End of build

A feature/fix is **not finished** when the code is written. It is finished when
the gate below has been executed (or an item is explicitly waived with a reason).

## Gate (in order)

1. **Typecheck** — `pnpm typecheck` (or package filter) green.
2. **Unit tests** — run the tests you touched / added; green.
3. **Kept smoke** — if the change has a regression risk (canvas camera, cream,
   deploy-critical UI), a Playwright or scripted probe must **exist and pass**,
   not merely be authored. Writing `e2e/*.spec.ts` without a green run ≠ done.
4. **Commit + push** — only when the user asked to ship / finish / PR; then push
   so Railway (or CI) can deploy.
5. **Live check** — when the job includes deploy or “live”, probe the deployed
   URL (or CI status) for the commit / behaviour. Code on `main` without a live
   check is incomplete if live was in scope.

## Hard rules

- Do **not** say “done”, “shipped”, or “Phase closed” if any in-scope gate step
  failed, hung, or was skipped.
- A hung webServer / e2e / curl is a **blocker**, not a footnote. Retry with
  `reuseExistingServer` (start API/web yourself) or fix the hang, then re-run.
- One-off probe scripts that get deleted are not a substitute for a kept smoke
  when the gap analysis called for CI/e2e.
- Prefer: fail the gate loudly over a green narrative with missing evidence.

## Canvas-specific (Workstream)

- Phase 0 cream/zoom: parchment outside camera + `aerial-image-slot`
  `data-hide-paper="1"` — covered by `e2e/canvas-cream-zoom.spec.ts`.
- View rotate: pointer/wheel must use inverse camera (`clientToBoardPct`); do
  not ship rotate without that path verified.
- **Camera chrome (gates B+C):** frosted / dock / HUD UI MUST render through
  `CameraChrome` (portals to `camera-chrome-root` sibling of `.zoomWorld`,
  stamps `data-camera-chrome`). Kept detector:
  `e2e/canvas-chrome-detector.spec.ts` — must stay at **zero**
  `[data-testid=zoom-world] [data-camera-chrome]` after zoom-out. Do not use
  `scale(1/--studio-zoom)` as a substitute. See `docs/STUDIO-STYLING-AND-UX.md`
  § Camera parenting.
- **Nested chrome portals:** a component rendered inside a `FrameDrawer` must
  NOT wrap itself in `CameraChrome` — the drawer already portals. A second
  portal escapes the drawer and drops the component on the drawing with whatever
  absolute offset its CSS still carries (this is what parked the Sheets strip
  mid-plan and ate elevation callout clicks). Cover:
  `e2e/elevation-callout-hit.spec.ts`.
- **Contrast:** `e2e/canvas-contrast-aa.spec.ts` must stay at zero WCAG AA text
  failures across all five modes. When touching ink tokens or any translucent
  chrome surface, run it — it flattens the composited background, so it catches
  what eyeballing a token value cannot.
